{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>YHWH your Elohim, He it is who passes before you.</b> With all Israel he speaks, and likewise he says to them at the end of the parashah: ״כי YHWH אלהיך הוא ההולך עמך״." "<b>But.</b> In my opinion, in the case of Joshua he mentioned 'YHWH your Elohim,' for that is the level of his prophecy; and so Onkelos translated: שכינתיה עבר קדמך — and this is the sense of ״YHWH your Elohim, He it is who passes before you,״ Joshua, he it is who passes before you. But in the case of Moses he mentioned the special Name, for that is the level of his prophecy; that is what Scripture says: ״לפניו ו-YHWH אמר אלי״ — and likewise it is written after it: ״כאשר דבר YHWH״ — that is, to me; for thus we find at the beginning of the parashah of Va'etḥanan (Deuteronomy 3:26): ״ויאמר YHWH אלי רב לך אל תוסף״ and so forth, ״וצו את יהושע״ and so forth, ״כי הוא יעבר לפני העם הזה״. And the language of the verses reveals the secret of the levels of each one: the face of Moses is as the face of the sun; the face of Joshua is as the face of the moon."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:52:30.652608794Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}